worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_code_tasks.js"
  ceiling 1417
  rationale "Browser twins of the issue #1177 code-task handlers that read pasted code: debugging (shifted quotient and, since 2026-10-07, loop bounds past the end, #1177 R1), explanation, review, test generation and refactoring. Each `handle*` function mirrors the Rust `handle_*` function of the same name in `rust/src/solver_handlers/` (same cues, same seed tables, same templates); each `try*` function is the slug-named binding the browser dispatcher runs, and passes the lowercased prompt as `normalized` exactly as the native dispatcher does (`rust/src/meta_method_dispatch.rs`). JavaScript-first twin of native handler keys (code_debugging, code_explanation, code_review, test_generation, code_refactoring), added under R997-R999 (2026-10-06); growth is the ported handler, not silent regrowth. Ceiling 1202 (#1177 R1, 2026-10-07) +62: the third seeded defect class, an assignment inside a parenthesized if/while condition (codeDebuggingLoneAssignment / codeDebuggingScanForConditionAssignment), twins of Rust lone_assignment / scan_for_condition_assignment. Ceiling moved 1202 to 1417 for issue #1177 R5 and R7 (2026-10-07): explanation lists every non-blank line with a Coverage line, reading keyword-headed, closing-brace, augmented-assignment and call rows from data/seed/meanings-code-structure-explanations.lino through one generic reader; test generation turns stated examples into cases through the seed test_example_relation map and refuses by name instead of emitting a smoke skeleton (twins of code_explanation.rs and test_generation.rs)."
